    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.integrable_gaussian_iff: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:72-74 assumes only 'h : ℝ → ℝ' and states the Gaussian/Lebesgue integrability equivalence, matching ledger:869 and claims.yaml:3122. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:117-120 discusses 'product Gaussian density' and absolute integrability, not this separate measure-conversion lemma; auxiliary mapping is honest."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.integral_gaussian_eq: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:81-83 assumes 'h : ℝ → ℝ' and equates the Gaussian integral with the density-weighted Lebesgue integral, exactly as ledger:870 and claims.yaml:3129 say. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:117-120 uses integration against the density without stating this separate conversion identity. No integrability assumption is incorrectly attributed to the Lean type."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.integral_mul_eq_integral_deriv: P:finite-gaussian-matrix",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:88-92 requires '∀ x, HasDerivAt f (f′ x) x' and integrability of f, xf, f′. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:116-120 uses polynomials, for which those conditions hold, and states 'E[g_k P(g)] = E[∂_k P(g)]'. Ledger:871 and claims.yaml:3136 explicitly describe the harmless generalized differentiable-function version."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.stdPi: P:finite-gaussian-matrix",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:115 defines 'Measure.pi fun _ => gaussianReal 0 1' for natural N. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:93-94 assumes 'independent real standard Gaussians', and :117-118 uses their product density. Ledger:872 and claims.yaml:3143 correctly identify the canonical joint-law model; arbitrary-space correspondence is proved separately."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.isProbabilityMeasure_stdPi: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:118-119 proves 'IsProbabilityMeasure (stdPi N)' without additional hypotheses, matching ledger:873 and claims.yaml:3150. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:94 implicitly uses a probability distribution but contains no separate labelled probability-instance assertion; auxiliary classification is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.integral_coord_mul_eq_integral_partial: P:finite-gaussian-matrix",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:126-131 requires every coordinate-slice derivative and 'Integrable f', 'Integrable (fun x => x k * f x)', and 'Integrable f′'. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:116-120 supplies these through polynomiality and Gaussian decay. Ledger:874 and claims.yaml:3157 accurately expose the generalized identity and its conditions, rather than supplying the manuscript's polynomial integrability."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.integrable_one_add_abs_pow: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:163-164 states, for 'd : ℕ', integrability of '(1 + |x|)^d' against N(0,1), matching ledger:875 and claims.yaml:3164. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:116-117 says Gaussian decay dominates every fixed power, but does not contain this particular envelope lemma. Its auxiliary designation is justified."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.one_add_norm_le_prod: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:175-176 assumes 'x : Fin N → ℝ' and proves '1 + ‖x‖ ≤ ∏ i, (1 + |x i|)', using the sup norm. Ledger:876 and claims.yaml:3171 say precisely this. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:116-120 does not use this explicit product-envelope inequality; the different-route auxiliary designation is correct."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.integrable_one_add_norm_pow: P:finite-gaussian-matrix",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:191-192 quantifies over natural 'N d' and proves integrability of '(1 + ‖x‖)^d' under stdPi. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:116-117 asserts 'All polynomial moments are finite because Gaussian decay dominates every fixed power'. Ledger:877 and claims.yaml:3178 accurately state the finite-dimensional polynomial-growth envelope implementing that assertion."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.integrable_of_growth: P:finite-gaussian-matrix",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:201-205 assumes 'AEStronglyMeasurable f' and '|f x| ≤ C * (1 + ‖x‖)^d', then proves integrability. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:116-120 uses polynomial functions, which satisfy those conditions. Ledger:878 and claims.yaml:3185 explicitly state the broader measurable-growth version; no stronger input is imposed on the final matrix result."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianIBP.integrable_coord_mul_of_growth: P:finite-gaussian-matrix",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "GaussianIBP.lean:208-211 assumes the same measurability and growth bound for f and concludes integrability of 'x k * f x'. TeX integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:116-120 needs precisely this integrability for polynomial P. Ledger:879 and claims.yaml:3192 accurately disclose the generalized sufficient hypotheses."
